WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.450
What breaks in production?

2
00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:06.256
Assuming Exposure Management in GCC
stalls attack-path work, and makes a Zero

3
00:00:06.256 --> 00:00:11.288
Trust Assessment test look failed; the
disposition and the interim path guard it.

4
00:00:11.288 --> 00:00:15.550
An exposed device with no owner
never gets patched; it's a finding.

5
00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:19.201
Sentinel queries on the
vulnerability tables return nothing,

6
00:00:19.201 --> 00:00:22.150
so the kit queries Defender's
own advanced hunting.

7
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.402
Reading only last month's incidents
misses an old one still open,

8
00:00:26.402 --> 00:00:28.488
so the active filter is read too.

9
00:00:28.488 --> 00:00:32.852
And a time to triage computed from
the wrong field is a precise-looking,

10
00:00:32.852 --> 00:00:36.140
wrong number, so the kit
reports past-window instead.
